node_modules/

# Fix round (Mars r1 follow-up, discovered while applying the four listed
# findings): the root .gitignore's bare `lib/` pattern matches a directory
# named `lib` at ANY depth, so it was silently excluding this package's own
# hand-authored `src/lib/` (pairing, tokenStore, eventsMapper, certPin,
# remoteApi, notify, lock, ring, qrDecode, capacitorStorage,
# backgroundSync) from every commit since this cell's very first one — the
# files existed on disk (so local tests/builds worked) but were never
# actually tracked. `git ls-tree -r HEAD --name-only | grep src/lib` was
# empty before this line. Un-ignoring here (not editing the root file,
# which other cells' own `lib/` build-output directories may legitimately
# rely on staying ignored) is the minimal fix.
!src/lib/
!src/lib/**

# Vite build output (Capacitor's webDir). Regenerated by `npm run build`;
# `npx cap sync` copies it into android/.../assets/public and ios/.../public,
# which — like the rest of the generated native projects — ARE committed.
www/
dist/
.DS_Store

# Capacitor-generated native projects: keep only the customizations we hand-author.
# (ios/ and android/ are committed once generated; native build outputs stay out.)
android/app/build/
android/.gradle/
android/local.properties
android/captures/
ios/App/Pods/
ios/App/build/
ios/App/DerivedData/
*.xcuserstate
